00:27:46.000 --> 00:28:18.000
in terms of working as psychologists in their community. So there's this entire branch of psychology that gets missed when we leave out these diverse kinds of voices. So I'm really hopeful that we can change that. And that historians, 100 years from now, will have a better archival record to work with when they want to tell those stories. And that realization, I think, led to the creation of the I. I am psyched traveling exhibition that you worked on with APA. I know I've seen that. It's been in our building. Do you want to talk about that for a moment?
在作为心理学家在社区中工作方面，做了如此多重大的工作。因此，当我们遗漏这些多样化的声音时，心理学的这整个分支就被遗漏了。所以我真的希望我们能改变这一点。而且100年后的历史学家在想要讲述这些故事时，将拥有更好的档案记录。而且这种认识，我认为，促成了你与APA合作创作的“我是心理学”（I Am Psyched）巡回展览。我知道我见过那个展览。它曾在我们的建筑里展出过。你想谈谈那个吗？

